# Railway

Railway is the only cloud target. Production-only — no staging.

## railway.toml

Project config lives in `railway.toml` (committed). It defines:
- `build` — Docker build command and Dockerfile path
- `deploy` — start command, healthcheck path, replicas
- `cron` — for batch jobs

Never configure these in the Railway dashboard. If a setting can't be
expressed in `railway.toml`, write an ADR explaining why and add a
comment in the dashboard pointing to the ADR.

## Env vars

Set via CLI for an audit trail:

```bash
railway variables --set DATABASE_URL=postgres://...
railway variables --set SENTRY_DSN=https://...
railway variables --set LOG_LEVEL=INFO
```

To dump all current vars: `railway variables`. Pipe through `gpg` if
you need to share them safely.

## Deploy

```bash
just deploy        # railway up
just deploy-status # railway status
just logs          # railway logs --json | jq
```

`just deploy` does:
1. Confirms working tree is clean (no uncommitted changes — but commits
   come AFTER smoke, so this is checking against the last commit).
2. Confirms tests pass locally (`just test`).
3. Runs `railway up`.
4. Waits for the deployment to become active.
5. Prints the public URL.

## Healthcheck

Every service exposes `/health`. Configure in `railway.toml`:
```toml
[deploy]
healthcheckPath = "/health"
healthcheckTimeout = 30
```

Railway will not route traffic to a deployment that fails the healthcheck.

## Rollback

If smoke fails:
```bash
railway redeploy --previous
```

This rolls to the prior deployment within seconds. Then debug locally,
not in prod.

## Migrations

Run as a Railway pre-deploy step:
```toml
[deploy]
preDeployCommand = "alembic upgrade head"
```

If migrations fail, the deploy aborts before promoting the new image.

## Logs

- `railway logs --tail` for live tail
- `railway logs --json` for structured (we emit JSON via structlog, so
  this is what you want for parsing)
- `railway logs --json | jq 'select(.level=="ERROR")'` for error filter

## Forbidden

- Setting env vars in the Railway dashboard (use CLI)
- Multiple environments (no staging — single-dev workflow)
- SSH-into-container debugging (containers run as a non-root user with
  a minimal surface; reproduce locally with `docker compose up`)
- Running migrations manually after deploy (use preDeployCommand)
